diff --git a/arma_CWR/engine/Poseidon/Graphics/Remaster/ITERATIONS.md b/arma_CWR/engine/Poseidon/Graphics/Remaster/ITERATIONS.md
index f47cfaa8..9de893f5 100644
--- a/arma_CWR/engine/Poseidon/Graphics/Remaster/ITERATIONS.md
+++ b/arma_CWR/engine/Poseidon/Graphics/Remaster/ITERATIONS.md
@@ -206,6 +206,14 @@ The owner saw the haze flicker in the trailer's dawn shot ("Moving out at dawn",
 - **Fix.** psFogInject turns the frame's jitter per cell with an interleaved-gradient offset of the cell, and in depth also per slice, so neighbouring cells' residuals are independent and average out. The sequence, the history share and the uniforms are unchanged. New test `[remaster][fog][Shaders]`.
 - **Result.** Valley band on the reshot clip: 0.567 to 0.103, 25076 spikes to 2 (vanilla 0.112). In play at 60 fps: 0.308 to 0.112. The look is unchanged apart from a hair more mist. Fog cells with no history (after a camera cut) may show cell-size speckle for a few frames; not seen in the clips.
 
+## F2. The fog wind (2026-10-23)
+
+The F1 fix stopped the pump but the owner saw "motion in the fog that makes it look like wind is blowing through it". A second board (`graphics-remaster/tmp/video/fogwind/`, not in git: eight Opus agents and three Fable agents) found two mechanisms and a fix.
+
+- **Cause.** The interleaved-gradient offset of a cell is a ramp over the cells (one cell to the right adds 0.556 of a slice), and the frame's golden-ratio step adds 0.618, so the next frame's offset field was this frame's read one cell over: the history's residual slid through the fog about one froxel cell (12 px) per render, in play and in the captures, in every region, with the camera held or moving. Any per-cell offset that is a lattice-periodic or linear function of the cell plus a frame-global step translates the same way. On top of that the history was read at the frame's jittered point, which made the stored value a leaky sum of the offsets (gain 1 / 0.12 = 8.3) instead of their average, and was the amplifier of the F1 pump.
+- **Fix.** psFogInject samples each cell at two fixed points (depth strata 1/4 and 3/4 of the slice, each weighted by the metres of its half slice, on the diagonal quarter points of the cell; `VolumetricFog.hpp` kFogTapZ, kFogTapXY) and never jitters, so the history has no residual to pump or to move; it is read at the cell's centre and is only a smoother of the light's own changes. The jitter uniforms stay 0 (the sequence still steps the near field's march). psFogIntegrate reads the injected volume through a 3 x 3 x 3 tent (eight trilinear taps half a cell and half a slice out): the jittered read used to blur the stored volume by about a cell, which is the mist's softness in the approved look (every centre-read variant without a blur was about 2 code values clearer in the valley); as a display filter the tent gives the same softness on a held and a moving camera and from the first frame after a cut, since nothing compounds through the history. Test `[remaster][fog][Shaders]` "fixed points": a mirror of the history over a cell grid measures the block-mean pump and the frame-to-frame travel of the residual at cell lags; the frame-wide offset trips the pump bar, the per-cell gradient the travel bar, the fixed taps neither.
+- **Result.** Stepped probes of the dawn valley (the fogwind kit, five regions, the per-cell F1 fix in brackets): with the camera held, the residual's travel correlation 0.04 (0.47), the in-place cell-scale change 0.048 (0.49) against the jitter-frozen floor 0.050, and the region means within 0.3 code values of the approved look (F1 +2.7 in the valley); on the real pan, wind 0.006 / 0.004 / 0.002 / 0.004 over bay / valley / far hill / haze against vanilla's 0.017 / 0.007 / 0.002 / 0.007 (F1 0.047 / 0.123 / 0.078 / 0.035), block flicker 0.059 against vanilla's 0.057 and the original's 1.62. Cost: one more medium and light sample per cell in the injection, eight trilinear reads instead of one fetch per step of the integration; the air stage's change is inside the contended machine's noise and needs the idle timing run of P1.
+
 ## P1. Pending
 
 - A clean timing run on an idle machine at 1080p, ideally on an RTX 3060.
